      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>References
     </subsection-heading>
     <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        rolemaps-to="Part"
       >
      <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
         xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
         Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
         rolemaps-to="P"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>The class makes various changes to the way that references are handled. Theclass loads natbib, and also the appropriate bibliography style. References canbe made using the normal method; the citation should be placed before anypunctuation, as the class will move it if using a superscript citation style.
       <text-fragment xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
          rolemaps-to="Span"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
        <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
          >
          <?References objects="1" ?>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>1
        </Reference>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>–
        <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
          >
          <?References objects="2" ?>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>4
        </Reference>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
       </text-fragment>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Theuse of natbib allows the use of the various citation commands of that package:
       <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
         >
         <?References objects="3" ?>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Abernethy et al.
       </Reference>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
       <text-fragment xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
          rolemaps-to="Span"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
       </text-fragment>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>have shown something, in
       <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
         >
         <?References objects="4" ?>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>1999
       </Reference>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
       <text-fragment xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
          rolemaps-to="Span"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
       </text-fragment>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>, or as given by Ref.
       <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
         >
         <?References objects="1" ?>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>1
       </Reference>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>. Longlists of authors will be automatically truncated in most article formats, butnot in supplementary information or reviews.
       <text-fragment xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
          rolemaps-to="Span"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
        <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
          >
          <?References objects="5" ?>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>6
        </Reference>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
       </text-fragment>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>If you encounter problems withthe citation macros, please check that your copy of natbib is up to date. Thedemonstration database fileachemso-demo.bib shows how to complete entriescorrectly. Notice that “et al.” is auto-formatted using the\latin command.
      </text-block>
     </semantic-para>
     <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        rolemaps-to="Part"
       >
      <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
         xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
         Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
         rolemaps-to="P"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Multiple citations to be combined into a list can be given as a single cita-tion. This uses the mciteplus package.
       <text-fragment xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
          rolemaps-to="Span"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
        <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
          >
          <?References objects="6" ?>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>7
        </Reference>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
       </text-fragment>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Citations other than the first of the listshould be indicated with a star. If the mciteplus package is not installed, thestandard bibliography tools will still work but starred references will be ignored.Individual references can be referred to using\mciteSubRef: “ref. 7.c”.
      </text-block>
     </semantic-para>
     <semantic-para xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        rolemaps-to="Part"
       >
      <text-block xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
         xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
         Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
         rolemaps-to="P"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>The class also handles notes to be added to the bibliography. These shouldbe given in place in the document.
       <text-fragment xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
          rolemaps-to="Span"
         >
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
        <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
          >
          <?References objects="7" ?>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>8
        </Reference>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>
       </text-fragment>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>As with citations, the text should be placedbefore punctuation. A note is also generated if a citation has an optional note.This assumes that the whole work has already been cited: odd numbering willresult if this is not the case.
       <text-fragment xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
          rolemaps-to="Span"
